From 93d9a4af976cd69e49cc0abced7a39486c20b173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVBridgeState: the tunnel signalled with the HDMI 1.4b vendor
 InfoFrame

The older Dolby Vision signalling that some displays ask for (the previous commit) is the tunnel of
the Standard mode with, in place of the Dolby vendor InfoFrame, the HDMI 1.4b one: OUI 00-0C-03,
24 bytes of payload, HDMI_Video_Format 1 (PB4 0x20) with the HDMI_VIC in PB5 for 3840x2160 at 30,
25 and 24 Hz (1, 2, 3; their 1000/1001 rates too) and 4096x2160 at 24 Hz (4), PB4 and PB5 0 in
any other mode, PB6 to PB24 0; and the AVI InfoFrame of the tunnel, with VIC 0 in the modes of an
HDMI_VIC. The drivers send it with a property of their own:

- the kernel backends (i915/xe, amdgpu): DVBRIDGE_DV_HDMI14B_LAB = 1 next to
  DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB, a modifier of the Standard tunnel as DVBRIDGE_DV_LOW_LATENCY_LAB is;
  the kernel makes both InfoFrames for the mode of each commit;
- nvidia-drm: NV_HDMI_DV_HDMI14B = 1 with that InfoFrame in NV_HDMI_VSIF_METADATA
  (nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9045, nvidia-legacy-open-9058), and "max bpc" 8, the default
  colorimetry and no HDR metadata, as for the Dolby one; NVKMS then sends AVI VIC 0, and refuses an
  InfoFrame whose HDMI_VIC is not that of the mode of the commit.

CDVBridgeState::Capture() takes it (hdmi14b): only where the driver has the property
(SupportsHdmi14b()), never with Low-Latency, which the drivers refuse with it. For nvidia-drm the
InfoFrame is that of the mode selected (DV_HDMI14B::Payload() of Hdmi14bVic(), in the new
DVHdmi14b.h, pure), and Stage() makes it again for the mode of a commit that changes it, so the
InfoFrame changes in the same commit as the mode; its blobs are kept while the output is captured
(a commit refused after a change of mode goes back to the blob of before), and restoring it puts
back what the connector had, the two properties together. A Kodi that ended with it set leaves
it to ClearLeftover(), which now resets those two properties as well.

Nothing calls it with hdmi14b yet: no output changes.

Tested on the host: the bytes for 27 timings of CTA-861
by their clock and totals (VIC 16, 31 to 34, 93 to 100, 114, 117, 118, interlaced and 3D),
"20 03", "20 02", "20 01" for VIC 93, 94, 95 and "00 00" for the others; each payload is the form
that NVKMS of nvidia-open-kernel-modules-9045 takes (its nvkms-hades.h built with the test), it
allows it with the HDMI_VIC of each mode, for a display with UHD_VIC and one without, and refuses
another one: 173 checks. Stage() and Capture() are compiled and read, not run: no DRM device on the
host.
